    "['xconnect vfi [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1.1 unit 0 family ccc', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `xconnect vfi LDP1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1.1 unit 0 family ccc\\nset routing-instances LDP1 instance-type l2vpn\\nset routing-instances LDP1 interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset routing-instances LDP1 route-distinguisher 1.1.1.1:1\\nset routing-instances LDP1 vrf-target target:1:1\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses a different paradigm where L2VPNs are configured as routing instances\\n2. The `ccc` (Circuit Cross-Connect) family is used for pseudowire connections\\n3. The VFI context from Cisco is translated to a routing instance in Juniper\\n4. You'll need to adjust the route-distinguisher and vrf-target values according to your specific network requirements\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1.1 unit 0 family ccc'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances LDP1 instance-type l2vpn', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `xconnect vfi LDP1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1.1 unit 0 family ccc\\nset routing-instances LDP1 instance-type l2vpn\\nset routing-instances LDP1 interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset routing-instances LDP1 route-distinguisher 1.1.1.1:1\\nset routing-instances LDP1 vrf-target target:1:1\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses a different paradigm where L2VPNs are configured as routing instances\\n2. The `ccc` (Circuit Cross-Connect) family is used for pseudowire connections\\n3. The VFI context from Cisco is translated to a routing instance in Juniper\\n4. You'll need to adjust the route-distinguisher and vrf-target values according to your specific network requirements\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances LDP1 instance-type l2vpn'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances LDP1 interface ge-1/0/1.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `xconnect vfi LDP1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1.1 unit 0 family ccc\\nset routing-instances LDP1 instance-type l2vpn\\nset routing-instances LDP1 interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset routing-instances LDP1 route-distinguisher 1.1.1.1:1\\nset routing-instances LDP1 vrf-target target:1:1\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses a different paradigm where L2VPNs are configured as routing instances\\n2. The `ccc` (Circuit Cross-Connect) family is used for pseudowire connections\\n3. The VFI context from Cisco is translated to a routing instance in Juniper\\n4. You'll need to adjust the route-distinguisher and vrf-target values according to your specific network requirements\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances LDP1 interface ge-1/0/1.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances LDP1 route-distinguisher 1.1.1.1:1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `xconnect vfi LDP1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1.1 unit 0 family ccc\\nset routing-instances LDP1 instance-type l2vpn\\nset routing-instances LDP1 interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset routing-instances LDP1 route-distinguisher 1.1.1.1:1\\nset routing-instances LDP1 vrf-target target:1:1\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses a different paradigm where L2VPNs are configured as routing instances\\n2. The `ccc` (Circuit Cross-Connect) family is used for pseudowire connections\\n3. The VFI context from Cisco is translated to a routing instance in Juniper\\n4. You'll need to adjust the route-distinguisher and vrf-target values according to your specific network requirements\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances LDP1 route-distinguisher 1.1.1.1:1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances LDP1 vrf-target target:1:1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `xconnect vfi LDP1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1.1 unit 0 family ccc\\nset routing-instances LDP1 instance-type l2vpn\\nset routing-instances LDP1 interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset routing-instances LDP1 route-distinguisher 1.1.1.1:1\\nset routing-instances LDP1 vrf-target target:1:1\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses a different paradigm where L2VPNs are configured as routing instances\\n2. The `ccc` (Circuit Cross-Connect) family is used for pseudowire connections\\n3. The VFI context from Cisco is translated to a routing instance in Juniper\\n4. You'll need to adjust the route-distinguisher and vrf-target values according to your specific network requirements\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances LDP1 vrf-target target:1:1'}]]": 1,
    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ndelete disable\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, in Juniper Junos, interfaces are enabled by default, so you could also simply remove any disable statement (the equivalent of \"no shutdown\"). The most direct translation would be:\\n\\n##\\ndelete disable\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Junos, you don\\'t typically need to explicitly enable interfaces like Cisco\\'s \"no shutdown\" since they are enabled by default. The \"delete disable\" would be used if the interface was previously disabled.', 'trans_template': 'delete disable'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ndelete disable\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, in Juniper Junos, interfaces are enabled by default, so you could also simply remove any disable statement (the equivalent of \"no shutdown\"). The most direct translation would be:\\n\\n##\\ndelete disable\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Junos, you don\\'t typically need to explicitly enable interfaces like Cisco\\'s \"no shutdown\" since they are enabled by default. The \"delete disable\" would be used if the interface was previously disabled.', 'trans_template': 'delete disable'}]]": 1,
